{"n": 1218, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1218.webp", "text": "730 64 326\n\n30 64 142\n\n64\n\nCheck operating condition of discharging and\ncharging equipment before using,\n\nCheck oil level and oil grade in compressor.\nAlso refer to operating instructions for\ncharging equipment.\n\nCaution!\n\nDo not subject pressure gage (2) to excessive\nPressure during procedures — danger of\ndestruction.\n\nNote:\n\nAn air conditioner could also be discharged and\ncharged with only one charging hose (high or\nlow pressure side),\n\nDischarging and charging procedures, however,\nare faster when carried out with a core valve\nremover and two charging hoses..\n\nAbsolute cleanliness is required for work on\nair conditioners.\n\nWear protective clothes.\n\nClose all valves on equipment before starting\nwork.\n\nFollowing jobs are only applicable to the\nillustrated charging station.\n\nRemove cap.\nConnect blue charging hose (1) on low pressure\nside (thick pipe) of air conditioner.\n\nRemove cap.\nConnect red charging hose (1) on high pressure\nside (thin pipe or drier) of air conditioner.\n\n7\n\n7\n#)\n¢\n7\n?\n7\n?\n7\n'\n?\n|\nf\n\ncbr y\n\n320 64 116\n\nConnect retrigerant bottle (2) and charging\nhose (16) with charging valve (1)\n\nCharging valve (1) remains closed until filling\nthe charging cylinder.\n\nOpen valves (4, 6 and 22)\n\nTurn on pump with switch (12) and discharge\nair conditioner.\n\nClose valve (22) and open valves (5 and 23)\nDischarge air conditioner\n\nOpen valve (25).\n\nOpen charging valve (1) and fill charging\ncylinder with refrigerant while air conditioner\nis being further discharged.\n\nRefrigerant and volume*.\n\n* See label in engine compartment.", "words": [["730", 0.1976, 0.2712, 0.2128, 0.2798], ["64", 0.2158, 0.2706, 0.2264, 0.2779], ["326", 0.231, 0.2692, 0.2467, 0.2779], ["30", 0.2047, 0.9682, 0.2148, 0.9748], ["64", 0.2194, 0.9688, 0.2295, 0.9761], ["142", 0.2345, 0.9688, 0.2472, 0.9761], ["64", 0.4681, 0.0186, 0.4924, 0.0411], ["Check"